WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.380
Prompt history can be valuable for improvement.

2
00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:17.880
Teams may use interaction records to evaluate answer quality, review hallucinations, tune retrieval, test safety controls, improve prompts, analyze feature adoption, prepare benchmark sets, or train and fine-tune models.

3
00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:24.220
These uses can make an AI product safer and more reliable, but reuse changes the purpose of the data.

4
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:32.000
A record collected to help a user continue a task should not automatically become training material or a broad analytics dataset.

5
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:36.360
Governed reuse starts with approval and purpose.

6
00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:49.660
The team should know which records are eligible, which are excluded, who approves reuse, what notice or consent is required where applicable, what classification limits apply, and how long the resulting dataset will live.

7
00:00:49.760 --> 00:01:04.480
Sensitive tenants, privileged communications, regulated content, children, employee records, source code, credentials, and confidential business material may require stricter rules or complete exclusion.

8
00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:08.120
Minimization still matters after data is selected.

9
00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:10.620
Raw conversations may not be necessary.

10
00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:21.840
Teams can use redaction, masking, aggregation, sampling, labeling, synthetic test cases, or metadata-only analysis when those approaches meet the goal.

11
00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:26.180
Tenant separation and user separation should be preserved.

12
00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:34.840
Dataset labels should describe source, purpose, sensitivity, owner, retention window, and restrictions on onward use.

13
00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:40.960
Teams should also separate raw operational logs from curated evaluation or training sets.

14
00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:47.860
Curated datasets need ownership, access control, quality review, deletion handling, and expiration.

15
00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:56.920
When prompt history is reused responsibly, improvement work becomes traceable and deliberate rather than an accidental secondary use of data that users did not expect.
